### Local values
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@orderServiceUrl = http://localhost:8081
@inventoryServiceUrl = http://localhost:8082
@sku = BK-001
@unknownSku = NO-SUCH-SKU
@customerId = customer-123
@quantity = 1
@orderId = PASTE_ORDER_ID_FROM_CREATE_RESPONSE
@rejectedOrderId = PASTE_REJECTED_ORDER_ID_FROM_CREATE_RESPONSE

### Gateway health
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### Order Service direct health
GET {{orderServiceUrl}}/actuator/health

### Inventory Service direct health
GET {{inventoryServiceUrl}}/actuator/health

### Read stock through Gateway
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/{{sku}}

### Unknown stock item through Gateway (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/{{unknownSku}}

### Reserve one unit directly through Inventory Service
POST {{inventoryServiceUrl}}/api/inventory/{{sku}}/reserve?quantity={{quantity}}

### Invalid inventory quantity (expect 400)
POST {{inventoryServiceUrl}}/api/inventory/{{sku}}/reserve?quantity=0

### Create an order through Gateway
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "sku": "{{sku}}",
  "quantity": {{quantity}}
}

### Retrieve the created order (replace @orderId above first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}

### Check the order's inventory reservation (wait for consumer log first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/reservations/{{orderId}}

### Check remaining stock through Gateway
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/{{sku}}

### Invalid order quantity (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "sku": "{{sku}}",
  "quantity": 0
}

### Create a valid order for an unknown SKU (expect 201, then async rejection)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "sku": "{{unknownSku}}",
  "quantity": 1
}

### Check the unknown-SKU reservation (replace @rejectedOrderId and wait for consumer log)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/reservations/{{rejectedOrderId}}
